1
00:00:00,980 --> 00:00:07,150
Zankoku na tenshi no you ni

2
00:00:00,980 --> 00:00:07,150
Just like the cruel angel

3
00:00:07,150 --> 00:00:15,110
Shounen yo shinwa ni nare

4
00:00:07,150 --> 00:00:15,110
Young boy, become a legend

5
00:00:18,990 --> 00:00:22,790
2D4U PRESENTS:

6
00:00:22,790 --> 00:00:26,000
Aoi kaze ga ima

7
00:00:22,790 --> 00:00:26,000
Even though the untested breeze...

8
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:29,800
mune no doa o tataitemo

9
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:29,800
...taps at the door to your heart

10
00:00:29,800 --> 00:00:37,470
Watashi dake o tada mitsumete hohoenderu anata

11
00:00:29,800 --> 00:00:37,550
You just look solely at me and smile

12
00:00:37,550 --> 00:00:44,730
Sotto fureru mono motomeru koto ni muchuu de

13
00:00:37,550 --> 00:00:44,730
So intent on seeking out that gentle touch

14
00:00:44,730 --> 00:00:52,070
Unmei sae mada shiranai itaike na hitomi

15
00:00:44,730 --> 00:00:52,070
Such innocent eyes, still ignorant of their destiny

16
00:00:52,070 --> 00:00:55,950
Dakedo itsuka kizuku deshou

17
00:00:52,070 --> 00:00:55,950
But someday, you are sure to realize...

18
00:00:55,950 --> 00:00:58,870
sono senaka ni wa

19
00:00:55,950 --> 00:00:58,870
...that upon your back

20
00:00:59,530 --> 00:01:03,160
Haruka mirai mezasu tame

21
00:00:59,530 --> 00:01:03,160
You have the wings with which to fly...

22
00:01:03,160 --> 00:01:06,830
no hane ga aru koto

23
00:01:03,160 --> 00:01:06,960
...towards the distant future

24
00:01:06,960 --> 00:01:10,960
Zankoku na tenshi no teeze

25
00:01:07,000 --> 00:01:10,960
The cruel angel's thesis

26
00:01:10,960 --> 00:01:14,630
Madobe kara yagate tobidatsu

27
00:01:10,960 --> 00:01:14,630
Soon, you will take flight from the windowsill

28
00:01:14,630 --> 00:01:18,470
Hotobashiru atsui patosu de

29
00:01:14,630 --> 00:01:18,470
With your torrent of ardent pathos

30
00:01:18,470 --> 00:01:21,970
Omoide o uragiru nara

31
00:01:18,470 --> 00:01:21,970
If you are to betray our memories

32
00:01:21,970 --> 00:01:25,730
Kono sora o daite kagayaku

33
00:01:21,970 --> 00:01:25,730
You, who embrace these heavens and shine

34
00:01:25,730 --> 00:01:29,770
Shounen yo shinwa ni nare

35
00:01:25,730 --> 00:01:29,770
Young boy, become a legend

36
00:01:30,400 --> 00:01:31,690
THE YEAR IS 2016 A.D.

37
00:01:31,730 --> 00:01:32,780
THE THING THAT PEOPLE HAD LOST

38
00:01:32,820 --> 00:01:34,280
IN OTHER WORDS, THE INSTRUMENTALITY
OF SOULS WAS STILL ONGOING

39
00:01:34,320 --> 00:01:36,400
HOWEVER, THERE IS FAR TOO LITTLE TIME LEFT
TO MAKE MENTION OF IT ALL

40
00:01:36,450 --> 00:01:38,160
THEREFORE, NOW, WE WILL TAKE
THE BOY NAMED SHINJI IKARI

41
00:01:38,200 --> 00:01:40,030
AND TELL THE STORY OF THE
INSTRUMENTALITY OF HIS SOUL

42
00:01:40,830 --> 00:01:42,330
IN THE CASE OF SHINJI IKARI

43
00:01:42,370 --> 00:01:43,040
FEAR

44
00:01:43,290 --> 00:01:45,580
Of ceasing to exist.

45
00:01:45,580 --> 00:01:48,670
But considering the way I am,
I don't think I need to exist.

46
00:01:48,670 --> 00:01:49,670
Why not?

47
00:01:49,670 --> 00:01:52,300
Because I'm not needed.

48
00:01:52,710 --> 00:01:55,630
I'm an unwanted child after all.

49
00:01:55,630 --> 00:01:57,510
No one cares about what happens to me!

50
00:01:57,510 --> 00:02:00,550
You're running away by thinking
that it doesn't matter.

51
00:02:00,550 --> 00:02:02,560
You're afraid of failure, aren't you?

52
00:02:02,560 --> 00:02:05,180
You're afraid that people won't
love you, aren't you?

53
00:02:05,180 --> 00:02:07,520
You're afraid of seeing how
weak you are, aren't you?

54
00:02:07,520 --> 00:02:09,810
But that's exactly how you are too, Miss Misato!

55
00:02:09,810 --> 00:02:12,860
That's right, we're all the same.

56
00:02:12,860 --> 00:02:14,690
There's a piece of our hearts missing.

57
00:02:14,690 --> 00:02:16,240
That's what we're afraid of.

58
00:02:16,240 --> 00:02:17,110
It makes us insecure.

59
00:02:17,110 --> 00:02:19,780
That's why we're all trying
to become one right now.

60
00:02:19,780 --> 00:02:21,950
We're trying to make up for it with each other.

61
00:02:21,950 --> 00:02:24,240
That is the Instrumentality Project.

62
00:02:24,240 --> 00:02:27,080
Humans cannot live unless they are in groups.

63
00:02:27,080 --> 00:02:29,540
Humans cannot live alone.

64
00:02:29,540 --> 00:02:31,790
Even though there is only one of you.

65
00:02:31,790 --> 00:02:33,630
That's why you suffer.

66
00:02:33,630 --> 00:02:35,210
That's why you feel lonely.

67
00:02:35,210 --> 00:02:38,470
That's why you want to meld your body
and soul with someone else's.

68
00:02:38,470 --> 00:02:40,260
You want to become one.

69
00:02:40,260 --> 00:02:43,220
Humans are made of weak and fragile stuff.

70
00:02:43,220 --> 00:02:46,890
The body and soul are also made
of weak and fragile stuff.

71
00:02:46,890 --> 00:02:50,020
That is why we must complement
one another through instrumentality.

72
00:02:50,020 --> 00:02:50,810
"WHY?"

73
00:02:51,310 --> 00:02:53,940
Because we cannot live otherwise.

74
00:02:53,980 --> 00:02:55,070
"REALLY?"

75
00:02:57,240 --> 00:02:58,780
What are you alive for?

76
00:02:58,820 --> 00:02:59,950
"I DON'T KNOW"

77
00:02:59,950 --> 00:03:03,030
Maybe I'm living because
I want to figure that out.

78
00:03:03,030 --> 00:03:04,830
Who are you living for?

79
00:03:04,830 --> 00:03:07,120
For myself, of course.

80
00:03:07,120 --> 00:03:08,870
For myself, I think.

81
00:03:08,910 --> 00:03:10,120
"REALLY?"

82
00:03:10,500 --> 00:03:12,670
Are you happy to be alive?

83
00:03:12,670 --> 00:03:14,090
I don't know.

84
00:03:14,090 --> 00:03:15,840
Are you happy to be alive?

85
00:03:15,840 --> 00:03:17,920
Of course, I'm happy!

86
00:03:17,920 --> 00:03:19,760
Are you happy to be alive?

87
00:03:20,090 --> 00:03:22,390
I only want to do what I enjoy doing.

88
00:03:22,390 --> 00:03:24,600
Do you hate feeling lonely?

89
00:03:24,600 --> 00:03:26,600
I don't like it.

90
00:03:26,600 --> 00:03:28,810
Do you hate suffering?

91
00:03:28,810 --> 00:03:30,560
I don't like it.

92
00:03:30,560 --> 00:03:32,270
Is that why you run away?

93
00:03:32,270 --> 00:03:33,270
That's right.

94
00:03:33,270 --> 00:03:36,190
What's wrong with running away
from the things you don't like?!

95
00:03:36,230 --> 00:03:37,530
Exit

96
00:03:36,520 --> 00:03:38,070
I shouldn't run away!

97
00:03:38,070 --> 00:03:40,240
Why mustn't you run away?

98
00:03:40,240 --> 00:03:41,990
Because running away is painful.

99
00:03:41,990 --> 00:03:44,320
Even though you're running away
from something painful?

100
00:03:44,320 --> 00:03:45,990
It was painful.

101
00:03:45,990 --> 00:03:49,250
If you know it's going to be painful,
then what does it matter?

102
00:03:49,250 --> 00:03:52,580
Yes, you can run away if it's painful.

103
00:03:52,580 --> 00:03:55,880
If you really hate it, you can run away.

104
00:03:55,880 --> 00:03:59,090
But I don't want to! I don't want
to run away anymore!

105
00:03:59,840 --> 00:04:02,090
That's right, it's wrong to run away.

106
00:04:02,090 --> 00:04:06,180
That's because you feel that it's
more painful to just run away.

107
00:04:02,130 --> 00:04:06,010
Play

108
00:04:02,130 --> 00:04:06,010
Messages

109
00:04:06,180 --> 00:04:08,890
Because you learned how painful
it is to run away.

110
00:04:08,890 --> 00:04:11,350
That's why you don't want to run away, isn't it?

111
00:04:11,350 --> 00:04:14,600
Because if I run away, no one will respect me.

112
00:04:14,600 --> 00:04:16,230
Don't forsake me.

113
00:04:16,230 --> 00:04:18,820
Please, don't forsake me!

114
00:04:18,820 --> 00:04:21,690
Quietly obeying what other
people tell him to do,

115
00:04:21,690 --> 00:04:23,740
maybe that's his survival mechanism.

116
00:04:23,740 --> 00:04:27,410
That's right! Because if I don't,
I'll be abandoned again.

117
00:04:27,410 --> 00:04:29,950
You're afraid of being hurt, aren't you?

118
00:04:29,950 --> 00:04:32,210
It's just what you've made
yourself believe, isn't it?

119
00:04:32,210 --> 00:04:34,750
Shinji, you're not the only one who's hurting.

120
00:04:35,290 --> 00:04:38,290
You're not the only one
goin' through tough times.

121
00:04:38,290 --> 00:04:41,460
You only believe that,
because it's easier to think that.

122
00:04:41,460 --> 00:04:44,300
Shut up! That has nothing to do with this!

123
00:04:44,300 --> 00:04:46,760
No one cares what happens to me!

124
00:04:46,760 --> 00:04:49,970
You're always so quick to
dismiss your self-worth.

125
00:04:49,970 --> 00:04:52,230
Because I have nothing.

126
00:04:52,230 --> 00:04:55,480
There you go again, making yourself
believe that you're worthless!

127
00:04:55,480 --> 00:04:59,020
Because if you believe that and
do nothing, you won't be hurt.

128
00:04:59,020 --> 00:05:02,650
You sustain your identity with the praise
you receive from people.

129
00:05:03,110 --> 00:05:05,570
No one will accept me.

130
00:05:05,570 --> 00:05:07,870
You've made yourself believe that.

131
00:05:07,870 --> 00:05:10,740
That's why I have to pilot the Eva.

132
00:05:10,740 --> 00:05:15,330
You've made yourself believe that
you are worthless to start with.

133
00:05:15,330 --> 00:05:17,380
That's what I have to do!

134
00:05:17,380 --> 00:05:18,960
That's not true.

135
00:05:18,960 --> 00:05:22,050
You've probably just made
yourself believe that.

136
00:05:22,050 --> 00:05:24,630
No, I am worthless.

137
00:05:24,630 --> 00:05:26,220
I have nothing to be proud of.

138
00:05:26,220 --> 00:05:28,340
That's why you pilot the Eva.

139
00:05:28,340 --> 00:05:31,260
By piloting the Eva, I can be me.

140
00:05:31,600 --> 00:05:35,020
By piloting the Eva, I can be me.

141
00:05:35,350 --> 00:05:38,520
I had nothing before I started piloting the Eva.

142
00:05:38,860 --> 00:05:42,320
I'm allowed to be here, because I pilot the Eva.

143
00:05:42,320 --> 00:05:44,400
I have nothing else.

144
00:05:44,820 --> 00:05:47,200
Because I have nothing else.

145
00:05:47,200 --> 00:05:50,120
I have nothing, nothing at all.

146
00:05:50,240 --> 00:05:51,580
"THAT MAKES MY LIFE WORTH SOMETHING"

147
00:05:51,950 --> 00:05:52,870
Nothing.

148
00:05:52,950 --> 00:05:54,500
"...SO"

149
00:05:54,910 --> 00:05:56,910
I hate myself.

150
00:05:58,420 --> 00:06:01,750
I hate you! I hate you! I hate you so much!

151
00:06:01,750 --> 00:06:04,090
Man, I just hate you!

152
00:06:04,090 --> 00:06:06,590
I hate who you are.

153
00:06:06,590 --> 00:06:09,140
I'm sorry, I hate you.

154
00:06:09,140 --> 00:06:10,140
I hate you.

155
00:06:10,140 --> 00:06:11,220
I do hate you.

156
00:06:11,220 --> 00:06:12,510
I hate you.

157
00:06:12,510 --> 00:06:14,640
I hate who you are.

158
00:06:14,640 --> 00:06:16,930
I hate the person you are.

159
00:06:16,930 --> 00:06:18,640
I just hate you!

160
00:06:18,980 --> 00:06:21,650
See? Everyone thinks so.

161
00:06:21,650 --> 00:06:23,730
Transfer Application
Shinji Ikari

162
00:06:22,270 --> 00:06:24,150
I know that's what they think.

163
00:06:24,150 --> 00:06:26,240
You're just making yourself believe that.

164
00:06:26,570 --> 00:06:29,820
No! Because I hate myself!

165
00:06:30,280 --> 00:06:33,450
So, you've made yourself believe that
everyone else thinks so too.

166
00:06:33,450 --> 00:06:36,660
I hate you!

167
00:06:33,450 --> 00:06:36,160
I hate you! I hate you! I hate you so much!

168
00:06:37,250 --> 00:06:39,420
But they still praise me.

169
00:06:39,420 --> 00:06:41,670
They'll praise me if I pilot the Eva.

170
00:06:42,040 --> 00:06:43,340
People praised me.

171
00:06:43,460 --> 00:06:44,590
"THAT'S WHY I'M HAPPY"

172
00:06:44,840 --> 00:06:46,170
People praised me.

173
00:06:46,260 --> 00:06:47,590
"BUT IT DOESN'T MAKE ME HAPPY"

174
00:06:48,220 --> 00:06:50,510
Which way do you really feel?

175
00:06:51,050 --> 00:06:52,720
I don't know.

176
00:06:52,720 --> 00:06:55,260
No, both ways are real.

177
00:06:55,260 --> 00:06:57,480
And that's why you pilot the Eva, isn't it?

178
00:06:57,480 --> 00:06:59,730
Because right now, the Eva is all I have.

179
00:06:59,730 --> 00:07:01,810
Because otherwise, you can't
maintain your identity.

180
00:07:01,810 --> 00:07:05,480
It's true, Eva Unit 01 is a part of who you are.

181
00:07:05,480 --> 00:07:09,400
But if you keep clinging to the Eva,
the Eva itself will become you.

182
00:07:09,400 --> 00:07:12,320
The Eva itself will become all you are.

183
00:07:12,320 --> 00:07:16,080
The real you will cease to exist.

184
00:07:16,080 --> 00:07:17,160
I don't care!

185
00:07:17,240 --> 00:07:19,750
I never had anything to begin with anyway!

186
00:07:19,750 --> 00:07:23,170
Even the cello lessons I used to take
all came to nothing.

187
00:07:23,170 --> 00:07:25,750
That's because you never took the
initiative to make something of it!

188
00:07:25,750 --> 00:07:28,170
But I can pilot the Eva now!

189
00:07:28,260 --> 00:07:31,550
And eventually, you won't be able
to do anything without the Eva.

190
00:07:31,550 --> 00:07:32,800
Like me.

191
00:07:32,930 --> 00:07:34,430
"WHY DO YOU PILOT THE EVA?"

192
00:07:34,850 --> 00:07:36,680
Because that is all I have.

193
00:07:36,720 --> 00:07:39,640
FINAL EPISODE

194
00:07:36,720 --> 00:07:39,640
THE BEAST THAT
SHOUTED LOVE
AT THE HEART
OF THE WORLD

195
00:07:43,560 --> 00:07:44,860
Rain...

196
00:07:45,560 --> 00:07:47,360
A depressing mood...

197
00:07:47,690 --> 00:07:49,570
It's like the mood I'm in.

198
00:07:49,570 --> 00:07:51,030
I don't like it.

199
00:07:51,030 --> 00:07:52,410
Sunset...

200
00:07:52,410 --> 00:07:54,200
Vanishing life...

201
00:07:54,200 --> 00:07:55,780
My wish...

202
00:07:55,780 --> 00:07:57,200
I don't like it.

203
00:07:57,200 --> 00:07:59,080
Morning...

204
00:07:59,080 --> 00:08:00,790
The start of today...

205
00:08:00,790 --> 00:08:02,870
The start of an unpleasant day...

206
00:08:03,170 --> 00:08:05,130
I don't like it.

207
00:08:05,130 --> 00:08:06,790
The blue sky...

208
00:08:07,210 --> 00:08:09,010
Something warm...

209
00:08:09,010 --> 00:08:10,630
Something I'm not used to...

210
00:08:10,630 --> 00:08:11,970
Something frightening...

211
00:08:11,970 --> 00:08:13,430
Something that's not needed...

212
00:08:13,430 --> 00:08:14,470
I don't like it.

213
00:08:14,890 --> 00:08:17,560
Everyone! I just hate everyone!

214
00:08:17,560 --> 00:08:18,720
What do you desire?

215
00:08:18,760 --> 00:08:19,770
"ARE YOU AFRAID OF BEING INSECURE?"

216
00:08:19,930 --> 00:08:21,350
What do you want?

217
00:08:21,390 --> 00:08:22,440
"DO YOU WANT PEACE OF MIND?"

218
00:08:22,690 --> 00:08:24,190
What do you seek?

219
00:08:24,230 --> 00:08:25,020
"DON'T HATE ME!"

220
00:08:25,020 --> 00:08:27,310
Don't hate me!

221
00:08:27,310 --> 00:08:28,320
What I'm afraid of is...

222
00:08:28,360 --> 00:08:29,150
REJECTION

223
00:08:29,440 --> 00:08:30,530
What I want is...

224
00:08:30,570 --> 00:08:31,740
TO CONNECT AND TO BE RECOGNIZED

225
00:08:31,990 --> 00:08:33,860
Is it okay if I stick around?

226
00:08:33,860 --> 00:08:35,610
Is it okay if I stay here?

227
00:08:35,610 --> 00:08:37,660
Do you love me?

228
00:08:37,700 --> 00:08:38,950
"DO YOU LOVE"

229
00:08:38,990 --> 00:08:40,120
"YOUR MOTHER?"

230
00:08:40,330 --> 00:08:42,830
Do you want to go to your mom?

231
00:08:42,830 --> 00:08:44,170
No, I don't want to.

232
00:08:44,170 --> 00:08:46,670
Aren't you going to go to your father?

233
00:08:46,670 --> 00:08:48,380
No, I don't want to.

234
00:08:48,380 --> 00:08:49,170
Why not?

235
00:08:49,210 --> 00:08:50,340
BECAUSE I'M AFRAID

236
00:08:50,760 --> 00:08:53,220
Because I'm afraid he'll hate me.

237
00:08:53,220 --> 00:08:55,800
Because I might cease to be me.

238
00:08:55,890 --> 00:08:56,840
"SO?"

239
00:08:57,260 --> 00:08:58,470
What do you desire?

240
00:08:58,510 --> 00:08:59,680
A RESOLUTION TO THE INSECURITY

241
00:09:00,060 --> 00:09:01,310
What do you seek?

242
00:09:01,350 --> 00:09:02,430
A RESOLUTION TO THE LONELINESS

243
00:09:02,730 --> 00:09:05,020
You're not happy, are you?

244
00:09:05,020 --> 00:09:07,350
I want something before that.

245
00:09:07,350 --> 00:09:09,860
I want to be worth something.

246
00:09:09,860 --> 00:09:13,280
Worth enough so no one will abandon me,
so they'll care about me.

247
00:09:13,320 --> 00:09:14,700
"I WANT TO BE WORTH SOMETHING"

248
00:09:15,150 --> 00:09:19,330
Only you can find your own worth.

249
00:09:19,370 --> 00:09:20,830
THAT'S WHY YOU PILOT THE EVA

250
00:09:21,290 --> 00:09:23,290
I'm worthless.

251
00:09:23,290 --> 00:09:25,460
My life isn't worth enough to live.

252
00:09:25,460 --> 00:09:27,960
Then, what are you?

253
00:09:27,960 --> 00:09:29,500
Then, what am I?

254
00:09:30,170 --> 00:09:31,960
What am I?!

255
00:09:35,130 --> 00:09:36,380
This is...

256
00:09:36,380 --> 00:09:37,510
Me!

257
00:09:37,510 --> 00:09:39,760
It's the form of me that I show to others.

258
00:09:39,760 --> 00:09:41,390
It's the symbol that is me.

259
00:09:41,390 --> 00:09:43,680
So is this, and this and this!

260
00:09:42,810 --> 00:09:43,470
SHINJI IKARI

261
00:09:43,680 --> 00:09:46,310
They're all just things that represent me.

262
00:09:46,310 --> 00:09:49,360
They're all merely what other people
recognize as me.

263
00:09:49,610 --> 00:09:51,360
Then, what am I?

264
00:09:52,070 --> 00:09:53,360
"WHERE DO I EXIST?"

265
00:09:53,440 --> 00:09:54,940
Is this me?

266
00:09:55,030 --> 00:09:56,200
The real me?

267
00:09:56,280 --> 00:09:57,570
The false me?

268
00:09:57,570 --> 00:09:59,320
You are you.

269
00:09:59,320 --> 00:10:01,780
The only thing is, there's a distinct
difference between that

270
00:10:01,780 --> 00:10:03,290
and the actual scope of who you are.

271
00:10:03,290 --> 00:10:04,410
That's right.

272
00:10:04,410 --> 00:10:05,660
My clothes...

273
00:10:05,660 --> 00:10:06,750
My shoes...

274
00:10:06,830 --> 00:10:08,330
My room...

275
00:10:08,330 --> 00:10:10,580
These things are a part of me.

276
00:10:10,580 --> 00:10:13,250
The things that are linked together
through your consciousness.

277
00:10:13,960 --> 00:10:16,470
The thing that I feel to be me, is me.

278
00:10:16,840 --> 00:10:19,340
I am nothing more than myself then.

279
00:10:19,640 --> 00:10:21,470
But I don't understand me.

280
00:10:22,010 --> 00:10:24,010
Where do I exist?

281
00:10:24,010 --> 00:10:25,930
What am I?

282
00:10:25,930 --> 00:10:27,600
What am I?!

283
00:10:27,770 --> 00:10:29,770
THAT IS WHY I
WISH FOR MY
SOUL TO BE
CLOSED OFF

284
00:10:30,100 --> 00:10:33,150
No one understands anything about me!

285
00:10:33,150 --> 00:10:36,650
What are you, stupid?! Of course,
no one understands!

286
00:10:37,150 --> 00:10:40,360
No one could possibly understand
anything about you!

287
00:10:40,360 --> 00:10:45,450
The only person who can sympathize
with you and understand you, is you.

288
00:10:45,830 --> 00:10:48,540
So, be good to yourself.

289
00:10:48,540 --> 00:10:53,420
But there's no me! I don't understand!

290
00:10:53,420 --> 00:10:55,000
There's no way I can be good to that!

291
00:10:55,050 --> 00:10:56,300
"YOU'RE INSECURE"

292
00:10:56,630 --> 00:10:58,630
In the end, you're insecure.

293
00:10:58,630 --> 00:11:00,300
The way you are now...

294
00:11:00,300 --> 00:11:02,850
The people around you now...

295
00:11:02,850 --> 00:11:05,260
The environment that surrounds you now...

296
00:11:05,890 --> 00:11:09,190
None of these things will last forever.

297
00:11:09,190 --> 00:11:11,650
Time will keep passing for you.

298
00:11:11,650 --> 00:11:14,980
Your world is made up of continual change.

299
00:11:14,980 --> 00:11:17,990
But above all, it's all up to your heart and mind.

300
00:11:17,990 --> 00:11:19,950
You can change the world at any time.

301
00:11:19,950 --> 00:11:21,490
What is this?

302
00:11:21,490 --> 00:11:23,280
A world with nothing in it?

303
00:11:23,280 --> 00:11:25,160
A world with nobody in it?

304
00:11:25,160 --> 00:11:27,040
A world of freedom.

305
00:11:27,040 --> 00:11:28,700
Freedom?

306
00:11:28,700 --> 00:11:32,880
It's a world of freedom, where there's
nothing restricting you.

307
00:11:33,380 --> 00:11:35,250
This is freedom?

308
00:11:35,250 --> 00:11:37,380
Yes, a world of freedom.

309
00:11:37,710 --> 00:11:40,130
But in exchange, there's nothing.

310
00:11:40,130 --> 00:11:42,010
As long as I don't think of anything?

311
00:11:42,010 --> 00:11:44,720
Yes, as long as you don't think of anything.

312
00:11:44,720 --> 00:11:48,310
But I don't know what I should do.

313
00:11:48,310 --> 00:11:49,640
You're insecure, aren't you?

314
00:11:49,640 --> 00:11:51,640
You don't have an image of yourself, do you?

315
00:11:51,640 --> 00:11:53,400
It's all just too vague.

316
00:11:53,400 --> 00:11:55,650
A world where there is nothing
solid enough to grab onto...

317
00:11:55,690 --> 00:11:56,900
THAT IS FREEDOM

318
00:11:57,690 --> 00:11:59,610
A world you can do anything you want with...

319
00:11:59,610 --> 00:12:02,200
But you're insecure, aren't you?

320
00:12:02,200 --> 00:12:05,030
Do you not know what you should do?

321
00:12:05,030 --> 00:12:06,700
What should I do?

322
00:12:06,700 --> 00:12:08,290
I will give you a restriction.

323
00:12:08,290 --> 00:12:10,700
There, now you have heaven and earth.

324
00:12:10,700 --> 00:12:13,960
But now, you've lost one aspect of your freedom.

325
00:12:13,960 --> 00:12:16,540
You must stand on the ground.

326
00:12:16,540 --> 00:12:19,000
But you feel more secure.

327
00:12:19,000 --> 00:12:21,720
Because a small weight has been
lifted from your mind.

328
00:12:21,720 --> 00:12:23,180
And you try walking.

329
00:12:23,180 --> 00:12:25,300
That is of your own will.

330
00:12:25,300 --> 00:12:27,550
This is my will?

331
00:12:27,550 --> 00:12:31,390
A ground exists in this world,
and that is the world you live in.

332
00:12:31,390 --> 00:12:34,400
But you can move around in it freely.

333
00:12:34,400 --> 00:12:37,520
If you wanted to, you could even change
the position of the world.

334
00:12:37,520 --> 00:12:41,570
And the position of the world
never stays still either.

335
00:12:41,570 --> 00:12:44,450
It changes, along with the passage of time.

336
00:12:44,450 --> 00:12:47,120
You yourself can change as well.

337
00:12:47,490 --> 00:12:52,710
Because what shapes you is your own mind
and the world around you.

338
00:12:53,040 --> 00:12:55,830
For, this is your world.

339
00:12:55,830 --> 00:12:59,040
It's the form of reality that you perceive.

340
00:12:59,090 --> 00:13:00,300
"THAT IS REALITY"

341
00:13:01,170 --> 00:13:02,720
This is...

342
00:13:02,720 --> 00:13:04,590
A space with nothing in it.

343
00:13:04,590 --> 00:13:06,640
A world with nothing in it.

344
00:13:06,640 --> 00:13:09,100
A world that has nothing else in it, except me.

345
00:13:09,510 --> 00:13:11,850
I'm losing my grasp on who I am.

346
00:13:12,220 --> 00:13:14,480
I feel like I'm disappearing.

347
00:13:14,810 --> 00:13:17,060
The existence that is me is vanishing.

348
00:13:17,310 --> 00:13:18,150
"WHY?"

349
00:13:18,150 --> 00:13:20,900
Because you are the only one here.

350
00:13:20,900 --> 00:13:22,650
Because I'm the only one?

351
00:13:22,650 --> 00:13:25,700
Because without the existence of
things other than yourself,

352
00:13:25,700 --> 00:13:27,700
you cannot know your own shape.

353
00:13:27,700 --> 00:13:28,870
My own shape?

354
00:13:28,910 --> 00:13:30,330
"MY IMAGE OF ME?"

355
00:13:30,330 --> 00:13:35,460
Yes, you know your own shape through
seeing how other people are shaped.

356
00:13:35,460 --> 00:13:37,620
By looking at the barrier between you
and other people,

357
00:13:37,620 --> 00:13:40,090
you visualize your own shape.

358
00:13:40,090 --> 00:13:43,920
You cannot see yourself unless
there are other people.

359
00:13:43,920 --> 00:13:47,050
I can exist because there are
other people around!

360
00:13:47,050 --> 00:13:50,140
If I'm alone, I'll always be alone,
no matter how far I go with it!

361
00:13:50,510 --> 00:13:53,140
All the world would just be me!

362
00:13:53,140 --> 00:13:55,850
By recognizing the differences
between yourself and others,

363
00:13:55,850 --> 00:13:58,150
you shape who you are.

364
00:13:58,150 --> 00:14:01,320
The very first other person is your mother.

365
00:14:01,320 --> 00:14:04,650
Your mother is a person separate from you.

366
00:14:04,650 --> 00:14:06,450
Right, I'm me.

367
00:14:06,740 --> 00:14:11,240
But it's also certain that the other people
shape my mind as well!

368
00:14:11,240 --> 00:14:13,540
That's right, Shinji Ikari.

369
00:14:13,540 --> 00:14:16,290
Did you finally figure that out, stupid Shinji?!

370
00:14:22,090 --> 00:14:25,300
So, you're finally awake, stupid Shinji.

371
00:14:25,300 --> 00:14:27,510
Oh, it's just you, Asuka.

372
00:14:28,760 --> 00:14:31,890
JUST me?! I come over here every morning

373
00:14:31,890 --> 00:14:34,470
to make sure that YOU aren't late to school,

374
00:14:34,470 --> 00:14:37,810
and those are the words of gratitude
you offer to your childhood friend?!

375
00:14:37,810 --> 00:14:39,600
Yeah, thanks.

376
00:14:40,150 --> 00:14:43,610
So let me sleep for a little longer.

377
00:14:44,650 --> 00:14:46,280
What kind of spoiled attitude is that?!

378
00:14:46,280 --> 00:14:48,110
Darn it, hurry up and get up!

379
00:14:53,450 --> 00:14:55,830
Pervert! Idiot! Letch! I can't believe you!

380
00:14:55,830 --> 00:14:58,540
I can't help it! It's morning!

381
00:15:00,960 --> 00:15:02,750
Oh, that Shinji.

382
00:15:03,040 --> 00:15:07,460
Asuka's being so nice, coming to get him.
He's just hopeless.

383
00:15:07,460 --> 00:15:08,760
Yes, Dear.

384
00:15:08,760 --> 00:15:13,220
You too! Stop burying your nose in that
newspaper and get ready to go.

385
00:15:13,220 --> 00:15:14,720
Yes, Dear.

386
00:15:14,720 --> 00:15:18,180
Honestly, a grown man and you're
no different than Shinji.

387
00:15:18,180 --> 00:15:20,310
Are you all ready to go?

388
00:15:20,310 --> 00:15:22,150
Yes, any time!

389
00:15:22,150 --> 00:15:24,730
I'm the one who gets scolded by
Professor Fuyutsuki

390
00:15:24,730 --> 00:15:26,900
when we're late to meetings, you know.

391
00:15:26,900 --> 00:15:28,940
You're just that popular.

392
00:15:28,940 --> 00:15:32,450
Don't be silly! Please hurry up and get dressed!

393
00:15:32,450 --> 00:15:33,740
Yes, Dear.

394
00:15:33,740 --> 00:15:36,450
South Pole Showa Base Opening Its Doors to visitors First African-American Female President

395
00:15:34,200 --> 00:15:36,450
I know, Yui.

396
00:15:37,790 --> 00:15:40,330
Come on, hurry up!

397
00:15:40,330 --> 00:15:42,750
Yeah, I know!

398
00:15:42,750 --> 00:15:44,210
You're such a pain, Asuka!

399
00:15:44,210 --> 00:15:45,710
What did you say?!

400
00:15:47,960 --> 00:15:50,510
Well, Mrs. Ikari, see you later!

401
00:15:51,010 --> 00:15:52,380
See you later.

402
00:15:52,380 --> 00:15:54,050
Okay, I'll see you later!

403
00:15:54,640 --> 00:15:57,970
Come on, Dear! When are you going
to put that newspaper down?!

404
00:15:57,970 --> 00:16:00,390
Yes, I know, Yui.

405
00:16:07,320 --> 00:16:10,110
I heard there's a transfer student
coming in today.

406
00:16:10,110 --> 00:16:14,820
Well, by next year, they'll have transferred
the capital here after all.

407
00:16:14,820 --> 00:16:16,700
There's going to be more
and more people coming.

408
00:16:16,700 --> 00:16:19,290
That's true. I wonder what she's like?

409
00:16:19,290 --> 00:16:21,330
I hope she's cute.

410
00:16:24,170 --> 00:16:26,080
Oh, I'm late! I'm late!

411
00:16:26,080 --> 00:16:29,670
It'd be pretty bad if I'm late
on my first day, right?!

412
00:16:42,140 --> 00:16:44,980
Sorry about that! I was seriously in a hurry!

413
00:16:45,190 --> 00:16:47,310
Really sorry about that!

414
00:16:52,030 --> 00:16:56,240
What are you, stupid?

415
00:16:52,860 --> 00:16:56,240
What?! So, did you see them?
That girl's panties?

416
00:16:56,620 --> 00:16:59,870
I didn't really see them, just a little flash.

417
00:17:01,500 --> 00:17:04,710
You sure are a lucky bastard!
And the day's just started!

418
00:17:05,960 --> 00:17:08,000
What's the big idea, Class Rep?!

419
00:17:08,000 --> 00:17:09,340
And what about you, Suzuhara?!

420
00:17:09,340 --> 00:17:12,340
What kind of stupid talk is this
to start the morning off with?!

421
00:17:12,340 --> 00:17:15,090
Come on, hurry up and go change
the water in the flower vase!

422
00:17:15,090 --> 00:17:16,180
It's your week, isn't it?!

423
00:17:16,180 --> 00:17:17,970
Man, you're such a pain!

424
00:17:17,970 --> 00:17:19,350
What did you say?!

425
00:17:19,850 --> 00:17:23,560
He's the type who's going to
end up getting whipped.

426
00:17:23,560 --> 00:17:25,230
So are you.

427
00:17:25,230 --> 00:17:27,730
Why am I the type that's going
to end up getting whipped?

428
00:17:27,730 --> 00:17:30,360
What? I call it like I see it.

429
00:17:30,360 --> 00:17:31,360
Why?!

430
00:17:31,360 --> 00:17:32,900
Just look at yourself!

431
00:17:32,900 --> 00:17:35,820
That's just because you never shut up!

432
00:17:35,450 --> 00:17:38,160
Man, it's so peaceful.

433
00:17:35,820 --> 00:17:38,160
Oh, be quiet, stupid Shinji!

434
00:17:42,410 --> 00:17:44,250
Hey, it's Miss Misato!

435
00:17:52,420 --> 00:17:55,510
Miss Misato's just awesome!

436
00:17:56,760 --> 00:17:59,890
What's with that stupid trio?! They're so dumb!

437
00:18:04,980 --> 00:18:06,600
Rise! Bow!

438
00:18:06,890 --> 00:18:08,230
Be seated!

439
00:18:08,810 --> 00:18:10,690
Rejoice, boys!

440
00:18:10,690 --> 00:18:13,650
Let me introduce the much-rumored
transfer student!

441
00:18:13,650 --> 00:18:16,030
I'm Rei Ayanami, nice to meet you.

442
00:18:17,400 --> 00:18:20,410
You! You're the panty-peeker
from this morning!

443
00:18:20,410 --> 00:18:22,740
Hey! That's not fair!

444
00:18:22,740 --> 00:18:24,750
You're the one who flashed them at Shinji!

445
00:18:24,750 --> 00:18:27,040
Who are you?! Leaping to his defense like that?!

446
00:18:27,040 --> 00:18:29,040
What are you, an item?!

447
00:18:29,670 --> 00:18:33,250
Pull Back

448
00:18:30,130 --> 00:18:33,250
We're just childhood friends! You annoying brat!

449
00:18:33,500 --> 00:18:36,920
Hey, we're in the middle of class!
Please be quiet!

450
00:18:36,920 --> 00:18:40,760
Come on, this sounds like fun.
I want to know too.

451
00:18:40,760 --> 00:18:42,470
Please continue.

452
00:18:48,810 --> 00:18:51,400
I get it, this is also a possible world.

453
00:18:52,020 --> 00:18:54,150
One possibility that's in me.

454
00:18:54,150 --> 00:18:56,610
The me right now is not exactly who I am.

455
00:18:56,610 --> 00:18:58,820
All sorts of me's are possible.

456
00:18:59,780 --> 00:19:03,660
That's right. A me that's not
an Eva pilot is possible too.

457
00:19:05,330 --> 00:19:09,370
When you think of it that way,
this world of reality isn't so bad.

458
00:19:09,370 --> 00:19:12,130
The world of reality might not be so bad.

459
00:19:12,130 --> 00:19:14,130
But I hate myself.

460
00:19:14,130 --> 00:19:18,340
It's you that perceives reality
as bad and unpleasant.

461
00:19:18,340 --> 00:19:21,760
It's you who's mistaken reality for the truth.

462
00:19:21,760 --> 00:19:24,680
Your perspective on reality and the
importance you place on reality,

463
00:19:24,680 --> 00:19:28,350
the slightest difference in these things will
greatly change the world inside your mind.

464
00:19:28,350 --> 00:19:30,810
There are as many truths as there are people.

465
00:19:30,810 --> 00:19:33,770
But there is only one truth for you.

466
00:19:33,770 --> 00:19:35,650
One made from your narrow
perception of the world

467
00:19:35,650 --> 00:19:38,530
and from information that was
altered to protect yourself,

468
00:19:38,530 --> 00:19:40,280
a warped truth.

469
00:19:40,280 --> 00:19:43,990
Well, one person's perception of the world's
bound to be tiny anyway.

470
00:19:43,990 --> 00:19:48,950
But people only have that tiny ruler
to measure their surroundings with.

471
00:19:48,950 --> 00:19:53,460
And you only try to see things through
the truths that other people have given you.

472
00:19:53,460 --> 00:19:55,710
On sunny days, you feel good.

473
00:19:55,710 --> 00:19:57,670
On rainy days, you feel down.

474
00:19:57,670 --> 00:20:01,130
Once you've been taught that, you make yourself
believe that's how you should feel.

475
00:20:01,130 --> 00:20:03,890
Even though pleasant things
can happen on rainy days too.

476
00:20:03,890 --> 00:20:06,930
It's a delicate thing that can be
completely transformed

477
00:20:06,930 --> 00:20:08,810
just by how you perceive something.

478
00:20:08,810 --> 00:20:11,100
The truth within people, that is.

479
00:20:11,600 --> 00:20:14,650
That's about how solid the truth is for humans.

480
00:20:14,650 --> 00:20:18,020
Though, that's what also makes people
seek a deeper truth.

481
00:20:18,020 --> 00:20:21,990
You are merely not used to
being loved by other people.

482
00:20:22,450 --> 00:20:26,740
So there's no need for you to constantly care
about what other people think of you.

483
00:20:27,330 --> 00:20:30,790
But doesn't everybody hate me?

484
00:20:30,790 --> 00:20:32,370
What are you, stupid?!

485
00:20:32,370 --> 00:20:35,420
You're just making yourself
believe that, that's all!

486
00:20:36,210 --> 00:20:39,090
But I hate myself.

487
00:20:39,460 --> 00:20:44,970
Anyone who hates himself can't
come to love and trust others.

488
00:20:45,800 --> 00:20:51,020
I'm a gutless, hypocritical, wimpy coward.

489
00:20:52,480 --> 00:20:55,440
See? If you understand yourself,
you can be kind.

490
00:20:56,150 --> 00:20:58,110
I hate myself.

491
00:20:59,400 --> 00:21:01,900
But maybe I can learn to love myself.

492
00:21:02,860 --> 00:21:05,200
Maybe it's okay for me to be here!

493
00:21:06,070 --> 00:21:08,700
That's right! I'm me, nothing more, nothing less!

494
00:21:10,200 --> 00:21:12,120
I'm me.

495
00:21:12,120 --> 00:21:13,080
I want to be me!

496
00:21:13,910 --> 00:21:15,460
I want to be here!

497
00:21:16,210 --> 00:21:18,130
And it's okay for me to be here!

498
00:21:32,810 --> 00:21:34,350
Congratulations!

499
00:21:34,350 --> 00:21:35,730
Congratulations!

500
00:21:35,730 --> 00:21:36,810
Congratulations!

501
00:21:36,810 --> 00:21:38,150
Congratulations!

502
00:21:38,150 --> 00:21:39,270
Congratulations!

503
00:21:39,270 --> 00:21:40,230
Congratulations!

504
00:21:40,230 --> 00:21:41,610
Congrats!

505
00:21:41,610 --> 00:21:42,530
Congratulations!

506
00:21:44,280 --> 00:21:45,610
Congratulations!

507
00:21:45,610 --> 00:21:46,910
Congratulations!

508
00:21:46,910 --> 00:21:48,110
Congratulations!

509
00:21:48,110 --> 00:21:49,410
Congratulations!

510
00:21:49,410 --> 00:21:50,660
Congratulations!

511
00:21:52,080 --> 00:21:53,370
Thank you.

512
00:21:53,410 --> 00:21:54,870
TO MY FATHER, THANK YOU.

513
00:21:54,910 --> 00:21:56,370
TO MY MOTHER, FAREWELL.

514
00:21:56,410 --> 00:21:58,380
AND TO ALL THE CHILDREN...

515
00:21:58,420 --> 00:22:01,630
CONGRATULATIONS!
